=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect09c-tetrads_2_activity_format/image_016.png)

- For each pair of genes, classify the tetrads as [PD]{color=#B47804}, [NPD]{color=#00A933} and TT, and tabulate the results as follows\:
- trp1 &#8211; met14 (t and m)
  - [PD\:]{color=#B47804} 235 + 215 + 46 = 496
  - [NPD\:]{color=#00A933} 230 + 220 + 54 = 504
  - [TT\:]{color=#A1467E} = 0
- For this pair of genes, [PD]{color=#B47804} = [NPD]{color=#00A933} and therefore, [trp1 and met14 are also unlinked.]{color=#FF4000}
- However, there are no [TT]{color=#A1467E} for trp1 and met14, which means that both genes are [closely linked to their respective centromeres]{color=orange}.

